\pard\qc\b\fs34 Ubitron Mobility Axiom\par
\pard\qc\b\fs28 Quick Start Guide\par
\pard\qc\fs20 Audience: Operators and supervisors\par
\pard\qc\fs20 Language: English\par
\pard\qc\fs20 Version 1.1\par
\pard\qc\fs20 Revision date: July 2026\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 1. What this guide is for\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard This short guide takes you from first sign-in to one successful live check on \b Operations\b0 .\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard Use it when you need to:\par
\pard 1. Sign in\par
\pard 2. Find an online device\par
\pard 3. Open live video\par
\pard 4. Use \b PTT\b0  once\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard For full day-to-day procedures, use the User Manual. For server install or network problems, ask your administrator.\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 2. Before you start\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard 1. You have the dashboard address from your administrator.\par
\pard 2. You have a username and password (or first-day install credentials from IT).\par
\pard 3. Chrome or Edge is available.\par
\pard 4. At least one body-worn camera is online if you want to test live video.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Login page]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 3. First sign-in\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b IMPORTANT \emdash New install only\par
\pard 1. On a brand-new server, the first username and password are typically \b global\b0  / \b global123\b0 .\par
\pard 2. Use them once only.\par
\pard 3. Mobility Axiom opens \b Change your password\b0 . You cannot keep the factory password.\par
\pard 4. New password rules: at least 12 characters, with upper case, lower case, a number, and a symbol.\par
\pard 5. After you save, sign in again with \b global\b0  and your new password.\par
\pard 6. \b global123\b0  stops working.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Open Chrome or Edge.\par
\pard 2. Enter the dashboard address from your administrator.\par
\pard 3. Enter \b Username\b0 .\par
\pard 4. Enter \b Password\b0 .\par
\pard 5. Choose \b Language\b0  if needed.\par
\pard 6. Click \b Sign in\b0 .\par
\pard 7. New install only: on \b Change your password\b0 , type the install password in \b Current password\b0 , set \b New password\b0  and \b Confirm new password\b0 , then click \b Save and continue\b0 .\par
\pard 8. New install only: sign in again with \b global\b0  and your new password.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard The main dashboard opens. You can see the top tabs.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Sign in form]\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Change your password]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 4. Main tabs\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard After sign-in, find these tabs (your role may hide some):\par
\pard 1. \b Operations\b0\par
\pard 2. \b Evidence & Docking\b0\par
\pard 3. \b Command Wall\b0\par
\pard 4. \b Centre Summary\b0\par
\pard 5. \b Video Conference\b0\par
\pard 6. \b Settings\b0\par
\pard 7. \b Analytics\b0\par
\pard 8. \b CAD / RMS\b0  (Computer-Aided Dispatch / Records Management) \emdash optional integration; licensed\par
\pard 9. \b Tactical\b0\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard First-day work usually starts in \b Operations\b0 .\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Top navigation with Operations highlighted]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 5. First-day goal\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard 1. Open the dashboard\par
\pard 2. Confirm one unit is \b Online\b0\par
\pard 3. Open one live view with \b Pin\b0\par
\pard 4. Use \b PTT\b0  once\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 6. Check online devices\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Open the \b Operations\b0  tab.\par
\pard 2. Look at the \b Devices\b0  list (device summary).\par
\pard 3. Find a device marked \b Online\b0 .\par
\pard 4. If none are online, stop and ask your administrator.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard You can name at least one online device.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Devices list with Online]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 7. Open one live video\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. In \b Devices\b0 , find an online device.\par
\pard 2. Click \b Pin\b0 .\par
\pard 3. Wait for the live panel to open on the map.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard Live video from that camera appears.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Notes\par
\pard 1. The device must be \b Online\b0 .\par
\pard 2. The picture may take a few seconds.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: Live pin panel open]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 8. Use PTT once\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Steps\par
\pard 1. Find the same online device.\par
\pard 2. Press and hold \b PTT\b0 .\par
\pard 3. Speak clearly.\par
\pard 4. Release \b PTT\b0 .\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Expected result\par
\pard Your voice goes out while you hold the button.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b Important\par
\pard Do not tap \b PTT\b0  quickly. Hold it while speaking.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: PTT on Devices row]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 9. PTT versus Call\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard 1. \b PTT\b0  = hold to talk, release to stop\par
\pard 2. \b Call\b0  = tap to start a voice call session\par
\pard 3. Use \b PTT\b0  for quick field direction\par
\pard 4. Use \b Call\b0  when your procedure needs a call session\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 10. SOS awareness\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard If an SOS appears:\par
\pard 1. Read the red SOS banner.\par
\pard 2. Open live video if needed (\b Pin\b0 ).\par
\pard 3. Check the map location.\par
\pard 4. Follow your local response policy (full steps are in the User Manual, including \b Acknowledge\b0 ).\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard [Insert screenshot: SOS banner]\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 11. Where to go next\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard 1. User Manual \emdash full operator workflows\par
\pard 2. Your administrator \emdash login address, accounts, devices offline, server problems\par
\pard 3. \b Settings\b0  \emdash only options your role allows; do not change server network settings unless you are trained and authorised\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 12. Common first-day problems\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard\b Cannot sign in / stuck on Change your password\par
\pard 1. Meet all password rules. You cannot keep \b global123\b0 .\par
\pard 2. If \b global123\b0  no longer works, use the new password you set.\par
\pard 3. Recheck username, password, and dashboard address.\par
\pard 4. Ask your administrator if the account is active.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b No online devices\par
\pard 1. Confirm the camera is powered on.\par
\pard 2. Ask your administrator to check registration.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b No live video\par
\pard 1. Confirm \b Online\b0 .\par
\pard 2. Click \b Pin\b0  again.\par
\pard 3. Wait a few seconds.\par
\pard 4. If it still fails, ask your administrator.\par
\pard\sa120\par
\pard\b PTT not heard\par
\pard 1. Hold \b PTT\b0 ; do not tap.\par
\pard 2. Confirm you selected the correct device.\par
\pard\sa360\par

\pard\b 13. One-minute daily start\par
\pard\b0\par
\pard 1. Click \b Sign in\b0 .\par
\pard 2. Confirm \b Language\b0 .\par
\pard 3. Open \b Operations\b0  and check online devices.\par
\pard 4. Open one live unit with \b Pin\b0  if required.\par
\pard 5. Confirm \b PTT\b0  readiness if your SOP requires it.\par
\pard\sa360\par

